Other posters have done a good job answering your specific questions
(including this one). However, I didn't see anyone point out that there's
a larger general principle at work here:

Any time you use a command which acts on an inventory object, you'll
get a prompt like:
   What do you want to <verb>? [xy or ?*]

What that's saying is:
   <verb> seems to make sense for inventory letters x and y.
   Press '?' to see what x and y are.
   Press '*' to see your whole inventory.
   Press any inventory letter (any at all, not just x or y) to
      <verb> that item.

Also, '$' is a special inventory letter which refers to your gold for
the purposes of commands.

There are a number of situations where it's to your benefit to perform
a command on a object which is not in the list of those which "seem
to make sense" for the command.

Experiment. You'll be surprised. TDTTOE.


